$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of phosphine 5 (0.54 g, 1.63
mmol, 2.1 eq) in dry and degassed DCM under N2 DMAP (0.20 g, 1.63 mmol,
2.1 eq) and DIC (0.20 g, 1.63 mmol, 2.1 eq) were sequentially added. The
mixture was stirred for approximately 5 min under N2 and the solution was
subsequently transferred to the resin. After incubation for 16 h, the
resin was then washed under N2 stream with dry DCM (6 x 2 min) and dried
under vacuum to constant weight. The resin was stored under an inert
atmosphere to prevent phosphine oxidation. Successful phosphine
incorporation was confirmed by appearance of the corresponding resonance
at ca. -6 ppm in the 31P NMR spectra. 31P NMR (121 MHz, DMF): &#x3B4;
-7.78 (s). Minute amounts (&lt; 5%) of oxide phosphine (signal at ca. 32
ppm) were detected. Final resin loading (due to resin mass increase) was
estimated in 0.34 mmol·g-1. A similar procedure was used to prepare
phosphine-functionalized PEGA resin. For the synthesis of the diluted
version of resin 7 (7-dil), the coupling of the initial amino acid was
effected using a mixture of Fmoc-Gly-OH and Boc-Gly-OH (1:9 in a molar
basis). Thus, AM-PS resin (2.0 g, 0.39 mmol·g-1) was treated with mixture
of Fmoc-Gly-OH (68 mg, 0.23 mmol, 0.3 eq), Boc-Gly-OH (0.37 g, 2.1 mmol,
2.7 eq), DIPEA (0.54 mL, 3.12 mmol, 4 eq) and TBTU (0.75 g, 2.34 mmol, 3
eq) in DMF. After disappearance of amino groups, the resin was then
washed with DMF (6 x 2 min) and DCM (4 x 2 min). Then Boc protecting
groups were removed by treatment with a 1:1 mixture of TFA-DCM for 1 h
and the resin was washed with DCM (4 x 2 min), 5% DIPEA in DCM and neat
DCM again (4 x 2 min). Free amino groups were capped by treating the
DMF-swollen resin with a Ac2O-Py mixture (10 eq each) for 1 h. The resin
was finally rinsed with DMF (6 x 2 min) and DCM (4 x 2 min). Phosphine
installation on the diluted resin was effected as described for 7.
&lt;PARA&gt; Procedure C (release as urea): The iminophosphorane-loaded
resin was swollen in a solution of with 3-methoxypropylisothiocyanate (5
eq) in dry DMF (approximately 8 mL per g resin) under N2 and heated under
&#x3BC;w irradiation at 60 &#x00B0;C (2 x 10 min). Then, the resin was
filtered and washed with DMF (6 x 2 min) to obtain the released
carbodiimide. The combined filtrates were concentrated, the residue was
dissolved in MeOH and a catalytic amount of AcOH-washed silica gel was
added. Then, the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 5
min and the solvents were then co-evaporated twice with water and the
resulting urea was freeze-dried.
6I-[N'-(3-methoxypropyl)ureido]-6-II-VII-hexaazido-6I-VII-heptadeoxy-2I-VII,3I-VII-tetradeca-O-methylcyclomaltoheptaose
(12). Monourea 12 was obtained from 3 (52 mg, 35 &#x3BC;mol, 2 eq) and
resin 7-dil (0.5 g, 35 &#x3BC;mol·g-1) using the catch-and-release
protocol as described in procedure C in 76% yield (21 mg). HPLC: tR =
12.9 min; 1H NMR (500 MHz, MeOD): &#x3B4; 5.29-5.15 (m, 7 H, H-1I-VII),
4.03 (m, 2 H, CH2O), 3.93-3.80 (m, 14 H, H-5I-VII, H-6aI-VII), 3.67-3.63,
3.56-3.51 (2 m, 45 H, OMe), 3.62-3.56 (m, 7 H, H-6bI-VII), 3.61-3.47 (m,
14 H, H-3I-VII, H-4I-VII), 3.24-3.21 (m, 7 H, H-2I-VII); ESI-MS: m/z
1617.6 [M + Na]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (stage 6), solid-supported reaction, amino acid
attached to aminomethyl polystyrene (AM-PS) (stage 2), stage 1 added in
stage 4 after stirred at RT for 1 hour (stage 4), sealed glass vial used
(stage 5), acetic acid washed silica gel used (stage 7)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Implementing the "Catch-and-Release" Concept into a Simple Method for
Regioselective Cyclodextrin Modification
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pflueger, Iris; Benito, Juan M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(10), 2354-2357

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME45 STEP1
