$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the thermal
rearrangement: To a solution of Et2O (50 mL) cooled in an ice/H2O bath
was added the allylic alcohol (5 mmol, 1.25 equiv) and Et3N (5 mmol, 1.25
equiv), followed by a solution of
2-chloro-5,5-dimethyl-1,3,2-dioxaphosphorinane or diethylchlorophosphite
(5 mmol, 1.25 equiv) in 5 ml Et2O. The solution was then allowed to stir
for 20 min and the precipitated Et3N•HCl was removed by filtration using
standard Schlenk techniques.6 The Et2O was removed under vacuum and the
residue was dissolved in 5 mL xylene. The solution was added dropwise to
a solution of benzyl azide or 4-methoxybenzyl azide (4 mmol, 1 equiv) in
2 mL xylene cooled in an ice-H2O bath. When allyl azide was used as a
reactant, an excess (3 equiv) was used due to the volatility this
material. The reaction mixture was slowly warmed to rt over 1 h, heated
to 80 °C for 1 h, then diluted with an additional 10 mL xylene and heated
at reflux for 4 h. Upon cooling, the reaction mixture was subjected to
flash chromatography (1:9 hexanes/EtOAc) for isolation of the
phosphoramidate product. Benzyl-(5,5-dimethyl-2-oxo-2λ5-[1,3,2]
dioxaphosphinan-2-yl)-(1-propyl-allyl)-amine (6c): Prepared following the
general procedure in 88% yield (1.19 g) from trans-2-hexen-1-ol and 75%
yield (1.01 g) from cis-2-hexen-1-ol as a colorless oil. 1H NMR: δ 0.66
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 0.80 (s, 3H), 1.18 (s, 3H), 1.09-1.21 (m, 2H),
1.36-1.51 (m, 2H), 3.71-3.84 (m, 3H), 4.12-4.26 (m, 2H), 4.36 (d, J =
11.0 Hz, 2H), 4.98-5.03 (m, 2H), 5.68-5.76 (m, 1H), 7.17- 7.20 (m, 1H),
7.22-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.33-7.35 (m, 2H); 13C NMR: δ 13.81,19.69, 20.98,
22.77, 32.04, 34.70, 47.79, 59.61, 76.37, 116.45, 127.22, 128.33, 138.50,
139.76; IR (film): 3066, 3029, 2961, 2933, 2874, 1456, 1257 cm-1; Anal
calcd for C18H28NO3P: C, 64.08; H, 8.36; N, 4.15. Found: C, 63.99; H,
8.19; N, 4.13.
