$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
2-Alkylidenepyrrolidines 4a-ad. To a THF solution (10 mL) of 3 was added
PPh3 (1.2 equiv) at 20 °C, and the reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h
at 45 °C. The solution was cooled to ambient temperature, and water (50
mL) was added. The organic and the aqueous layers were separated, and the
latter was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 50 mL). The combined organic layers
were extracted with brine, dried (Na2 SO4), and filtered, and the solvent
of the filtrate was removed in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography (silica gel, ether/petroleum ether = 1:2 or
ether/petroleum ether = 1:5 → 1:2) to give pyrrolidine 4. Methyl
(Z)-(4-hydroxy-3,4,5-trimethylpyrrolidin-2-ylidene)acetate (4g):
Treatment of 3g (0.16 g, 0.70 mmol) with PPh3 yielded 4g as a yellow oil
(0.11 g, 75%, diastereomeric mixture); a small amount of
triphenylphosphane oxide could not be separated. 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3,
major isomer): δ = 1.09 (d, 3 J = 8 Hz, 3 H, CHCH 3), 1.21 (d, 3 J = 8
Hz, 3 H, CHCH 3), 1.23 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.58 (q, 3 J = 8 Hz, 1 H, CHCH3),
3.56 (q, 3 J = 8 Hz, 1 H, NCHCH3), 3.63 (s, 3 H, OCH3), 4.48 (s, 1 H,
=CH). 13C NMR (50.3 MHz, CDCl3, major isomer): δ = 8.5, 12.6, 20.7, 48.9,
50.1, 61.8, 76.7, 77.8, 130.7, 170.9. IR (neat): υ = 3378 (w), 3322 (br,
w), 2973 (w), 2952 (w), 2923 (w), 2860 (w), 1736 (s), 1614 (m), 1558 (m),
1486 (w), 1436 (s), 1381 (w), 1297 (m), 1180 (s), 1119 (s), 1094 (m),
1020 (w), 722 (m), 696 (w), 541 (m) cm−1. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 199
(M+, 1), 181 (25), 122 (100), 120 (7), 107 (6), 77 (3). The exact
molecular mass m/z = 199.1208 ±2 ppm [M+] for C10H17NO3 was confirmed by
HRMS (EI, 70 eV).
