$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(2-Aminoethylamino)-1-oxyl-2,2,5,5-tetramethyl-2,5-dihydro-
1H-imidazole 19. PBu3 (0.96 mL, 3.5 mmol) was added under argon to a
stirred solution of 10 (0.5 g, 2.25 mmol) in dry THF (10 mL). After the
vigorous N2 evolution had ceased, the reaction mixture was stirred for an
additional 30 min. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, 20 mL
of the aqueous C2H5OH solution (1:1) was added to the residue, and the
reaction mixture was allowed to stay under stirring at ambient
temperature for 6 h. C2H5OH was distilled off under reduced pressure, the
water layer was acidified with 3% HCl to pH 4 and extracted with CHCl3 (5
x 5 mL), and the organic layer was discarded. The water layer was
neutralized (NaHCO3) and extracted with CHCl3 (5 x 5 mL); the organic
layer was discarded again. The water layer was basified (NaOH) to pH 12
and extracted with CHCl3 (7 x 5 mL), then the organic layer was dried
over K2CO3. Solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give 19 as
yellow crystals (0.33 g, 1.67 mmol, 75%). yellow crystals.mp 66-68 °C dec
(hexane/EtOAc, 1:1); IR (KBr, cm-1) 3365 (NH2), 1626 (C=N), 1549 (NH).
Anal. Calcd for C9H19N4O•0.75H2O: C, 50.82; H, 9.65; N, 26.35. Found: C,
51.18; H, 9.39; N, 26.09.
