$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
{η5-C5H4-(PPh2dN-2,6-Me2-C6H3)}Fe{η5-C5H3-1-PPh2-2-CH(Me)NMe2} (1a). To a
solution of BPPFA (1.00 g, 1.60mmol) in diethyl ether (15 mL) was added
drop wise an equimolar amount of 2,6-dimethylbenzoyl azide (0.24 g,
1.60mmol). Bubbles of N2 gas evolved during the addition. Themixture was
further stirred overnight at ambient temperature, after which time the
solvent was removed. The oily residue dissolved in a minimum amount of
CH2Cl2 was transferred onto a column of silica gel for chromatographic
separation. A single orange band was eluted with a mixture of hexane
andethyl acetate (8:2) to give orange solids after removal of solvents.
Re crystallization from CH2Cl2/hexane yielded 0.49g of 1a in two crops as
yellow solids.
{η5-C5H4-(PPh2=N-2,6-Me2-C6H3)}Fe{η5-C5H3-1-(PPh2=N-2,6-Me2-C6H3)-2-CH(Me)NMe2}
(2a). The title compound was prepared by essentially the same method as
for the preparation of 1a, except for the use of an excess of
2,6-dimethylbenzoyl azide (1.14 g, 9.60 mmol) as compared with the amount
of BPPFA (1.00 g, 1.60 mmol). The product was obtained as yellow solids
after chromatographic separation (silica gel; hexane/ethyl acetate, 8/2).
Yield: 1.03 g (75%). 31P NMR (CDCl3): δ -7.72, -6.12 (s, P=NAr). 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ 0.91 (d, J = 6.7, 3H, CHMe), 1.49 (s, 6H, NMe2), 2.02, 2.04
(s, 12H, Me2C6H3), 4.12 (qt, J = 7.2, 1H, CHMe), 4.05-4.23 (m, 4H, C5H4),
4.20-4.96 (m, 3H, C5H3), 6.58 (t, J = 9.9, 2H, p-C6H3), 6.90 (t, J = 9.9,
4H, M-C6H3), 7.31-7.61 (m, 20H, C6H5). Anal. Calcd for C54H55FeN3P2: C,
75.08; H, 6.42; N, 4.86. Found: C, 75.26; H, 6.26; N, 4.67.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reaction, product depends on stoichiometry
