$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
2-Alkylidenepyrrolidines 4a-ad. To a THF solution (10 mL) of 3 was added
PPh3 (1.2 equiv) at 20 °C, and the reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h
at 45 °C. The solution was cooled to ambient temperature, and water (50
mL) was added. The organic and the aqueous layers were separated, and the
latter was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 50 mL). The combined organic layers
were extracted with brine, dried (Na2 SO4), and filtered, and the solvent
of the filtrate was removed in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography (silica gel, ether/petroleum ether = 1:2 or
ether/petroleum ether = 1:5 → 1:2) to give pyrrolidine 4. Methyl
(Z)-(4-hydroxy-3,5-dimethyl-4-phenylpyrrolidin-2-ylidene)acetate (4w):
Treatment of 3w (0.15 g, 0.49 mmol) with PPh3 yielded 4w as a yellow oil
(0.09 g, 75%, diastereomeric mixture, 3 stereocenters). 1H-NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3, major isomer): δ = 0.70 (d, 3 J = 7 Hz, 3 H, CHCH 3), 1.18 (d, 3 J
= 7 Hz, 3 H, CH 3CHNH), 3.44 (q, 3 J = 7 Hz, 1 H, CHCH3), 3.66 (s, 3 H,
OCH3), 3.86 (q, 3 J= 7 Hz, 1 H, CH3CHNH), 4.60 (s, 1 H, CH CO), 7.26 -
7.46 (m, 5 H, Ph), 7.98 (br, 1 H, NH). 13C-NMR (50.3 MHz, CDCl3, major
isomer): δ = 9.4, 18.9, 42.9, 50.3, 64.5, 77.0, 80.3, 126.3, 128.0,
128.6, 139.68, 166.50, 170.10. IR (neat) υ = 3420 (m), 3394 (w), 1735
(w), 1650 (s), 1605 (s), 1449 (w), 1322 (w), 1250 (s), 1199 (m), 1172
(m), 1126 (e), 1062 (w), 988 (w), 764 (w), 700 (w) cm-1. MS (EI, 70 eV):
m/z (%) = 261 (M+, 37), 230 (10), 156 (100), 124 (14), 105 (49). The
exact molecular mass m/z = 261.1365 ± 2ppm [M+] for C15H19NO3 was
confirmed by HRMS (EI, 70 eV). Anal. calcd for C15H19NO3 (261.14): C
68.91, H 7.19, N 5.55; found C 68.62, H 7.04, N 5.24.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
