$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 6-Triphenylphosphazo-1H-phenalen-1-one (Ic).
To a solution of 1.11 g (5 mmol) of azide Ib in 25 ml of methylene
chloride was added dropwise at stirring 1.5 g (5.7 mmol) of
triphenylphosphine in 25 ml of methylene chloride. The mixture was heated
under reflux for 1 h, then the solvent was removed in a vacuum and the
residue was heated with 40 ml of hexane for removing triphenylphosphine
excess. The crude product was chromatographed on silica gel (eluent
chloroform). Compound IIIc, yield 74%. mp 139-141°C, Rf: 0.48 (1), 0.72
(2), 0.44 (3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of triphenylphosphazoperiindenones by Staudinger reaction
