$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Triphenylphosphine (4a) (0.262 g, 0.001mol)
was added to 3 under N2 atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred at
65-70°C for 4 h and the progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC
using ethylacetate: n-hexane (2:3) as an eluent. After completion of the
reaction, the solvent was removed from the reaction mixture in a
rotaevaporator to get the crude product and it was purified by column
chromatography using ethylacetate:nhexane (1:4) to obtain pure product,
N-(1,3-Benzothiazol-2-ylmethyl)-N-(1,1,1-triphenyl-λ5-phosphanylidene)
amine (5a). The same procedure was adopted for the synthesis of remaining
title compounds and the physical data of these compounds are summarized
in Table 1. N -(1,3-benzothiazol-2-ylmethyl)- N
-(1,1,1-triphenyl-λ5-phosphanylidene)amine (5a) Dimethyl
N-benzo[d]thiazol-2-ylmethyl-P-phenyl phosphonimidate (5d) Pale brown
semi solid, Yield 68%. IR (υmax, cm-1): 3039 (C-H aromatic) (W), 1559
(C=C aromatic) (M), 1441 (P-Ph) (M), 1242 (P=N) (S), 1027 (P-O-C) (S),
978 (P-N) (S), 680 (C-H) (M); 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 8.14 (d, 1H,
J = 8.0 Hz, Ar-H), 7.99 (d, 1H, J = .6 Hz, Ar-H), 7.73 (d, 2H, J = 8.0
Hz, Ar-H), 7.59-7.45 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 3.76 (s, 6H, -OCH3), 2.54 (s, 2H,
-CH2-); 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 168.2 (C-2), 152.6 (C-8), 135.1
(C-3), 132.7 (C-2′ & C-6′), 131.4 (C-4′), 128.9 (C-1 ′), 128.3 (C-3′ &
C-5′), 125 (C-6), 124.1 (C-5), 122.2 (C-4), 121.6 (C-7), 41.2 (C-7′),
31.7 (C-1); 31P NMR (161.9 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ 31.3; ESI-Ms m/z (%): 333
[M+H]+ (55), 316 (100), 302 (90); Anal.Cald.for C16H17N2O2PS; C: 57.82,
H:5.16, N:8.43; Found: C:57.76, H:5.09, N:8.36.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
