$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Reaction of
1,3-Dicarbonyl Compounds 1a-o with α-Azidoketones 2a-f. To a solution of
diisopropylamine (2.6 equiv) in anhydrous THF (35 mL) was added n-BuLi
(2.6 equiv, 23 or 15% solution in hexane) at 0 °C. After stirring for 15
min, the dicarbonyl compound 1 (1.1 equiv) was added, and the solution
was stirred for 1 h at 0 °C. A THF solution (5 mL) of azidoketone 2 (1.0
equiv) was added at -78 °C, and the reaction mixture was warmed to
ambient temperature over a period of 12 h. After stirring for an
additional 3 h at 20 °C, a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl (50 mL)
was added, the organic layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was
extracted with Et2O (2 × 70 mL) and with CH2Cl2 (2 × 50 mL). The combined
organic layers were extracted with brine, dried (Na2SO4), and filtered,
and the solvent of the filtrate was removed in vacuo. The residue was
purified by chromatography (silica gel, ether/petroleum ether ) 1:4 →
1:3) to give the azido alcohol 3 as a diastereomeric mixture. Due to its
instability, the product should be used for further transformations
within 24 h. Ethyl (Z)-(4-hydroxy-4-phenylpyrrolidin-2-ylidene)acetate
(4r): Treatment of 3r (0.28 g, 0.96 mmol) with PPh3 yielded 4r as a
yellow solid (0.18 g, 73%, contains 5r). 1H-NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
1.15 (t, 3 J = 7 Hz, 3 H, OCH2CH 3), 2.43 (br, 1 H, OH), 2.87 (d, 2 J =
16 Hz, 1 H, CH2C=), 3.16 (d, 2 J = 16 Hz, CH2C=), 3.79 (d, 2 J= 13 Hz, 1
H, CH 2NH), 3.88 (d, 2 J = 13 Hz, 1 H, CH 2NH), 4.12 (q, 3 J = 7 Hz, 2 H,
OCH 2CH3), 4.65 (s, 1 H, CH), 7.30 - 7.54 (m, 5 H, Ph), 7.90 (br, 1 H,
NH). 13C-NMR (50.3 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.6, 47.4, 58.7, 60.9, 78.8, 79.1,
125.1, 127.9, 128.3, 142.16, 163.47, 170.58. IR (neat) υ = 3335 (m), 2978
(w), 1710 (s), 1646 (m), 1526 (w), 1449 (m), 1298 (w), 1195 (m), 1073
(w), 1029 (w), 811 (w), 761 (m), 695 (m) cm-1. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) =
247 (M+, 30), 229 (40), 156 (100), 142 (33), 105 (41). The exact
molecular mass m/z = 247.1208 ± 2 ppm [M+] for C14H17NO3 was confirmed by
HRMS (EI, 70 eV).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger-aza-Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-Alkylidenepyrrolidines and Pyrroles by Condensation of
1,3-Dicarbonyl Dianions with α-Azidoketones and Subsequent Intramolecular
Staudinger-Aza-Wittig Reaction
