$DATUM 1-[3,5-Bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-3-{(2S)-3,3-dimethyl-1-[(triphenylphosphoranylidene)amino]butan-2-yl}thiourea,
4a To azide 2 (300 mg, 0.726 mmol) in Et2O (1.8 mL) under argon
atmosphere was added triphenylphosphine (190 mg, 0.726 mmol) at rt.
Stirring was maintained at rt for 26 h and the reaction mixture was then
concentrated in vacuo to afford a colorless foam. Pentane (4 mL) was
added under N2 and the mixture stirred vigorously for 2 h. The resultant
suspension was filtered and the precipitate dried in vacuo. Compound 4a
(344 mg, 73%) as a colorless solid. [α]D 24 = - 64.4 (c = 1.40, CHCl3);
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 0.96 (s, 9H), 3.04 (‘q’, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H),
3.41 (‘t’, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H), 3.76 (br s, 1H), 7.32 - 7.80 (m, 19 H); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 27.1, 33.7, 48.0, 69.9 (d, J CP = 21.0 Hz),
116.5, 123.2 (q, J CF = 272.8 Hz), 123.4, 128.1, 128.9 (J CP = 12.4 Hz),
130.9 (q, J CF = 33.4 Hz), 132.5 (d, J CP = 9.5 Hz), 143.5, 183.7; 31P
NMR (202 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm 21.9 (br s); 19F NMR (470 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm -
62.7; IR νmax/cm-1 2970, 1739, 1437, 1367, 1216; MP 96 - 99 °C; HRMS
(ESI+): calcd. for C33H33F6N3PS [M+H]+ 648.2032, found 648.2024.
