$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of 3b (16.6 mg, 0.0440 mmol) in
0.5 mL 3:1 DMF-phosphate buffer was added a solution of 4 (6.50 mg, 0.049
mmol) in the same solvent 0.4 mL at room temperature. After 30 min, conc.
HCl was added to the reaction flask (total c = 6 M). The deprotection was
monitored completed within 20 min. The reaction mixture was transferred
into a sep-funnel and diluted with water. The mixture was extracted with
EtOAc one time. The aqueous layer was adjusted to pH 8-9 with 10% NaOH,
and then extracted with ethyl acetate twice (2 × 10 mL). The combined
organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo
to afford a desired amine. Compound 13 was synthesized following the same
protocol for compound 12. Without extraction, the crude product was
subjected to flash column chromatography on silica gel with 20 to 30%
MeOH in DCM to obtain a white solid (72 % yield). mp 149-153 °C; 1H NMR
(300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.71 (d, J= 8.1 Hz, 1H), 8.28 (m, 1H), 7.72 (m, 1H),
7.48 (m, 1H),7.26 (m, 5H), 5.26 (s, 1H), 4.34 (m, 1H), 4.25 (s, 2H), 3.90
(m, 1H), 3.90 - 3.71 (m, 2H), 3.09 (m, 2H), 2.53 (s, 3H), 2.24 (m, 1H),
1.98 (m, 1H), 1.65 - 1.38 (m, 3H), 0.97 - 0.75 (m, 6H); MS (ESI) m/zcalcd
for C21H33N4O4 [M+H]+ 405.3, found 405.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phosphate buffered solution used, Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
