$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Anilido-3-(het)aryl-2,7-dimethyl-5-phenyl-2,5-dihydro-1H-pyrazolo[4,3-c][1,5,2]diazaphosphinine
1-Oxides (20) To a stirred solution of compound 8 (2 mmol) in pyridine
(30 mL), anhyd MeOH (0.08 mL, 2 mmol) and arylazide (2 mmol) were added.
The mixture was maintained at 50 °C until nitrogen evolution had ceased
and then pyridine was evaporated in vacuo. The residue was triturated
with H2O and crystallized from i-PrOH. 20c, yield 72%. Mp: 206-208 °C;
31P NMR, δ (solvent): 5.3 (py); 1H NMR, δ : 2.20 [s, 3 H, CH3(Cl)C6H3NH],
2.50 (s, 3 H, CH3), 3.53 (d, 3JPH = 9.9 Hz, 3 H, NCH3), 6.30 (dd, 3JHH =
9.0 Hz, 4JHH = 3.0 Hz, 1 H, Ar), 6.67 (d, 4JHH = 3.0 Hz, 1 H, Ar), 6.93
(d, 3JHH = 9.0 Hz, 1 H, Ar), 7.10 (dd, 3JHH = 4.8 Hz, 3JHH = 3.9 Hz, 1 H,
Ar), 7.32 (t, 3JHH = 7.5, 1 H, Ar), 7.41-7.54 (m, 4 H, Ar), 7.70 (br d,
2JPH = 7.8 Hz, 1 H, NH), 8.02 (d, 3JHH = 9.0 Hz, 2 H, Ar)d.
