$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ethyl
2-(Acylamino)-4-fluoro-3-hydroxyoctadecanoates 7 and 8; General Procedure
Under an argon atmosphere, the respective 4-nitrophenyl alkanoate (0.75
mmol, 3 equiv) was added to a soln of ethyl
2-azido-4-fluoro-3-hydroxycarboxylate 5 or 6 (96 mg, 0.25 mmol) as a pure
diastereomer in THF-H2O (9:1, 20 mL) followed by addition of Ph3P (196
mg, 0.75 mmol, 3 equiv). The mixture was stirred at r.t. overnight. Then
Et2O (60-80 mL) was added and the soln was washed with sat. Na2CO3 soln
(3 × 20 mL) until the organic phase was colorless. The organic phase was
dried (MgSO4) and the solvent was evaporated. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography [cyclohexane-EtOAc, 1:1 (7a, 8a) or
cyclohexane-EtOAc, 5:1 (7b-d and 8b-d)]. Ethyl
2-(Dodecanoylamino)-4-fluoro-3-hydroxyoctadecanoate [(2R,3S,4S)-7d],
Yield: 0.100 g (71%). mp 88 °C. [α]D20 -19.9 (c 0.98, CHCl3). 1H NMR
(300.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.88 (t, 3JH,H = 6.5 Hz, 6 H), 1.29 (t, 3JH,H =
7.1 Hz, 3 H), 1.26-1.64 (brm, 42 H), 1.72-1.85 (m, 2 H), 2.26 (t, 3JH,H =
7.3 Hz, 2 H), 3.92 (dm, 3JH,F = 21.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.24 (dq, 3JH,H = 7.0 Hz,
3JH,H = 1.22 Hz, 2 H), 4.54 (dddd, 2JH,F = 48.8 Hz, 3JH,H = 8.6 Hz, 3JH,H
= 4.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.76 (dd, 3JH,H = 8.1 Hz, 3JH,H = 3.9 Hz, 1 H), 6.40 (d,
3JH,H = 8.1 Hz, 1 H). 13C NMR (75.48 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.0, 14.1, 24.9,
25.5, 22.7, 24.9, 29.2, 29.3, 29.4, 29.5, 29.6, 31.9, 31.1, 36.5, 54.5,
62.0, 73.5 (d, 2JC,F = 19.4 Hz), 94.2 (d, 1JC,F = 170.2 Hz), 169.8,
173.7. 19F NMR (282.37 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -195.62 (dddd, 2JF,H = 49.2 Hz,
3JF,H = 33.2 Hz, 3JF,H = 21.4 Hz, 3JF,H = 5.0 Hz, 1 F). HRMS (ES+): m/z
[M + Na]+ calcd for C32H62FNNaO4: 566.4555 found: 566.4555.
