$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the Staudinger/aza-Wittig reaction:
Triphenylphosphine (157 mg, 0.6 mmol) was added under nitrogen to a
solution of the corresponding Ugi adduct 5a-y (0.4 mmol) in toluene (10
ml) and the mixture was stirred for 24 h at room temperature. Then the
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue was
purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt mixtures as eluent).
Spectral assignations in NMR were performed from DEPT, COSY, HMQC and
HMBC experiments on 6a and DEPT experiment on 6c, both in CDCl3, as model
compounds.
N-Cyclohexyl-4-benzyl-5-oxo-2-phenyl-3,4-dihydrobenzo[e][1,4]diazepine-3-carboxamide
6a, (128 mg, 71%), colorless crystals (hexane/AcOEt),. mp 168-169 °C, 1H
NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.92 (dd, J = 1.5 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H, HAr),
7.72-7.69 (m, 2H, HAr), 7.45-7.16 (m, 11H, HAr), 5.22 (s, 1H), 5.15 (d, J
= 14.3 Hz, 1H), 5.03 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 4.43 (d, J = 14.3 Hz, 1H),
3.16-3.06 (m, 1H), 1.38-0.89 (m, 8H), 0.50-0.35 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100MHz,
CDCl3) δ 167.3 (Cq), 164.5 (Cq), 164.4 (Cq), 146.2 (Cq), 137.8 (Cq),
136.4 (Cq), 132.0 (CHAr), 131.0 (CHAr), 130.6 (CHAr), 129.2 (CHAr), 128.9
(CHAr), 128.7 (CHAr), 128.5 (CHAr), 127.5 (CHAr), 127.1 (CHAr), 126.1
(CHAr), 125.8 (Cq), 59.2 (CH), 52.7 (CH2), 47.9 (CH), 32.2 (CH2), 32.0
(CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 24.5 (CH2), 24.3 (CH2); IR (KBr) ν̃ 3297 (NH), 3057
(CHAr), 2948, 2856, 1652 (C=O), 1532, 1451; EIMS m/z 451 (M+, 8), 327
(24), 326 (100), 325 (16), 235 (40), 91 (59); HRMS (EI) calcd for
C29H29N3O2: 451.2260; found 451.2260; Anal. Calcd for C29H29N3O2: C,
77.13; H, 6.47; N, 9.31. Found: C, 76.98; H, 6.59; N, 9.41.
