$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(3):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Glycosyl Amides 11g-11i and 12g-12h. The phosphine (4g-4i; 1.2 mol equiv)
was added, at room temperature and under argon, to a solution of the
azide 5r or 6r (1 mol equiv) in a mixture of toluene and DMA 3:1 (0.1 M).
The solution was heated to 70 °C and stirred for 4 h. The disappearance
of the starting material was monitored by TLC (8:2 toluene/acetone). Then
water was added, and the mixture was stirred for 18 h at the same
temperature. The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure, and the
crude was purified by flash chromatography.
Nα-t-butoxycarbonyl-Nγ-(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-benzyl-α/β-D-galactopyranosyl)-
L-asparagine-O-benzyl Ester (12h). Flash chromatography: 70:30
hexane/AcOEt; α/β ratio 68:32; yield = 71%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3; α):
6.22 (d, NH, J1-NH = 6.5 Hz), 5.71 (dd, H1, J1-2 = 4.5 Hz, J1-NH = 6.5
Hz). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3; β): 5.39 (d, NH, J1-NH = 9.0 Hz), 4.99 (dd,
H1, J1-2 = 8.4 Hz, J1-NH = 9.0 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, isomer mix.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Traceless Staudinger Ligation of Glycosyl Azides with Triaryl Phosphines:
Stereoselective Synthesis of Glycosyl Amides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bianchi, Aldo; Bernardi, Anna
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(12), 4565-4577

