$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
N,N-Diarylamidines 7 and 8 The solution of azide 1m (1.0 mmol) and
triphenylphosphine (1.0 mmol) in DCE (8 mL) was stirred under nitrogen
atmosphere at room temperature for 4 h. After cooled to -5 °C, Et3N (1.0
mmol) was added. Then the solution of azide 1a or 1i (1.0 mmol) and
phenoxyacetyl chloride 2b (1.0 mmol) in DCE (5 mL) was added dropwise at
-5 °C over 1 h. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for
0.5 h. The mixture was filtered to remove triethylamine hydrochloride and
the filtrate was evaporated in vacuum. Purification through a silica gel
column (hexane/EtOAc=16:1) gave a mixture of amidines 7 and 8 7b+8b, m.p.
123-124°C; IR (KBr): 3410, 1649, 1594, 1545, 1509, 1483, 1241 cm-1; 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.76 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 0.45 H), 8.29 (s, 0.45 H),
7.71 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1.1 H), 7.42 (s, 0.6 H), 7.39 (t, J = 8.5 Hz, 1.1
H), 7.27 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2.2 H), 7.18 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 0.7 H), 7.08 (d, J
= 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 6.98-6.96 (m, 1 H), 6.90-6.88 (m, 0.6 H), 6.80-6.79 (m,
2.8), 4.62 (s, 0.9 H), 4.53 (s, 1.1H), 2.27 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 155.3, 155.2, 151.7, 151.1, 147.5, 145.9, 137.8, 136.1, 132.2,
132.1, 130.5, 130.4, 130.2, 129.5, 129.1, 129.0, 128.3, 127.8, 125.9,
124.0, 123.3, 122.6, 122.4, 121.5, 120.8, 115.1, 115.0, 65.1, 64.3, 20.7;
MS: m/z 385 (M+H); HRMS: m/z calcd for (C21H18Cl2N2O+H) 385.0869, found
385.0860.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective Synthesis of 4-Alkylidene-β-lactams and N,N'-Diarylamidines
from Azides and Aryloxyacetyl Chlorides via a Ketenimine-Participating
One-Pot Cascade Process
