$DATUM 11,17
-Di-tert-butyl-12-methyl-2-phenylimino-3,2-oxaphospha-12-phosphoniapentaeyclo[11.5.1.0
2, 11 .0 4 , 1 0 . 12, 16]nonadeea-4(10),5,8,14,1 -pentaen-19-one Iodide
(12): Method A: A solution of 8a (210 mg, 0.33 mmol) and phenyl azide
(9b; 111 mg, 0.93 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was heated at 130 °C for 3 h in
a Schlenk pressure tube and then allowed to cool. After removal of the
solvent and the excess of 9b under vacuum (200e; 0.001 mbar) the residue
was washed with Et2O and toluene, and purified by recrystallization from
CH2Cl2 at - 3 °C to furnish 12. Pale yellow crystals, yield: 169 mg, 70%.
mp 216-219°C (dec). IR (KBr): v = 2958, 2886, 1722 (C=O), 1594, 1498,
1392, 1365, 1134, 842, 756 cm -1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): b = 1.24 Is, 9H, C
17-C(CH3 )3)' 1.57 [br s, 9H, C 11-C(CH3M 2.26 [ddd, 2J(H, H) = 13.0,
3J(H, H) = 6.5,6.5,1 H, H 7-ax), 2.83 [d, 2J(H, P 12) = 12.2, 3 H, P
12-CH3)' 2.87 [ddd, 2J(H, H) = 13.0, 3J(H, H) = 7.8, 7.8, 1 H, H 7-eq),
4.09 [dd, 2J(H, P 12) = 6.5, 3J(H, H) = 6.5, 1 H, H 13/16), 4.53 [dd,
ZJ(H, P 2) = 27.5, 3J(H, H) = 9.7,1 H, H 1), 5.55 [m, 3J(H, H) = 9.7, 1
H, H 18), 5.62 [ddd, 3J(H, H) = 9.7,7.8,6.5,1 H, H 6/8),5.90 [ddd, 3J(H,
H) = 8.0, 7.8, 6.5, 1 H, H 6/8), 6.07 [dd, 2J(H, P 12) = 11.0, 3J(H, H) =
4.2, 1 H, H 13/16), 6.21 [ddd, 3J(H, P 12) = 22.5, 3J(H, H) = 6.5,6.5, 1
