$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Ac4GalNDAz (7) To a solution of 3 (100 mg, 0.26 mmol) in THF
: water (2.58 mL, 9:1) was added 10 (96 mg, 0.26 mmol) at room
temperature. The reaction was allowed to stir overnight at room
temperature for 12 h. After the reaction appeared complete, the solvent
was evaporated to yield the crude product, which was purified by silica
gel column chromatography (40% EtOAc in hexanes, Rf = 0.4 in 60%
EtOAc/hexanes) to yield the product, 7 whose NMR matched the literature
reports.5 Yield 82 mg, 0.18 mmol, 70%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.72 (d,
J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 5.56 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1H), 5.37 (ddd, J = 3.4, 1.2, 0.5
Hz, 1H), 5.11 (dd, J = 11.3, 3.3 Hz, 1H), 4.42 (dt, J = 11.2, 9.1 Hz,
1H), 4.14 (qd, J = 11.2, 6.5 Hz, 2H), 4.04 (td, J = 6.5, 1.2 Hz, 1H),
2.17 (s, 3H), 2.13 (s, 3H), 2.04 (s, 3H), 2.02 (s, 3H), 1.91-1.85 (m,
2H), 1.81-1.74 (m, 2H), 1.01 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.6,
170.9, 170.6, 170.3, 169.7, 93.0, 72.0, 70.4, 66.5, 61.5, 49.9, 30.7,
29.3, 25.6, 21.1, 20.8, 20.2; IR (film) 3280, 3075, 2920, 1751, 1675,
1549, 1439, 1370, 1220, 1120, 1072, 1042 cm-1.
