$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Glycosyl Azide Ligation with Aspartate or
Peptide (General Procedure). A solution of aspartic acid thioester 8,
dipeptide thioester 12, or tripeptide thioester 14 (0.02 mmol) and
glycosyl azide 7 or 10 (0.02 mmol) dissolved in dry DMF (2.0 mL) was
stirred at rt overnight under an argon atmosphere. TLC showed that the
reaction was completed. Then, Et2O (20 mL) was added to the reaction
mixture, and the resultant precipitates were collected and subjected to
purification by flash column chromatography or preparative TLC.
tert-Butyl
N-fluorenylmethyloxycarbonyl-glycinyl-Nγ-{2-acetamido-2-deoxy-β-D-glucopyranosyl-(1→4)-[2,3,4-O-tribenzyl-α-L-fucopyranosyl-(1→6)]-2-acetamido-3-O-benzyl-2-deoxy-β-D-glucopyranosyl}-L-asparaginate
13 . [α] = -18.0 (0.5, CHCl3); 1H NMR (CD3OD, 400 MHz): 7.75 (d, J = 7.6
Hz, 2H, Fmoc), 7.62 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H, Fmoc), 7.36-7.21 (m, 24H), 5.01
(d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H, H-1), 4.91 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H, H-1), 4.65 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 1H, H-1), 4.18 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H, Fmoc), 2.71 (dd, J = 16.4, 5.2
Hz, 1H, β-H of Asp), 2.61 (dd, J = 16.4, 5.2 Hz, 1H, β-H of Asp), 1.95
(s, 3H, Ac), 1.87 (s, 3H, Ac), 1.39 (s, 9H, t-Bu), 1.08 (d, J = 6.4 Hz,
3H, Fuc-Me); FAB MS: calcd. for C75H90N5O20 (M + H+): 1381; found 1381.
