$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Reactions between
Trimethyl Phosphite and 4 or 33. A solution of 4 or 33 (0.5 mmol) and
trimethyl phosphite (2.5 mmol, 5.0 eq.) in dry DCM (12 mL) containing
either of 1H-tetrazole (2.5 mmol, 5.0 eq.), acetic acid (2.5 mmol, 5.0
eq.), pyridine (2.5 mmol, 5.0 eq.), or DBU (2.5 mmol, 5.0 eq.), or none
of them was stirred at rt and the reaction was monitored by TLC. Upon the
completion of reactions (6-36 h), the mixture was concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was then applied to flash column
chromatography to afford products shown in Schemes 2 and 5. Product 14
Product 15 Product 17 Product 34 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.78 (dd, J =
12.3, 2 H), 4.74 (dd, J = 11.3, 2 H), 4.63 (d, J = 3.9, 1 H), 4.55 (s, 2
H),4.05 (t, J = 5.5, 1 H) 3.80 (m, 2 H), 3.60 (m, 3 H), 3.62 (d, J = 1.5,
3 H), 3.58 (d, J = 1.5, 3 H), 3.40 (s, 3 H), 2.73 (t, J = 10.1, 1 H).
