$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of BnNDAz (4) To a solution of PhosDAz (3, 100 mg, 0.26 mmol)
in THF : water (2.5 mL, 9:1) was added benzyl azide (34.3 mg, 0.26 mmol).
The reaction was allowed to stir at room temperature for 12 h at which
point all of the starting material had been consumed. The solvent was
evaporated to yield the crude product which was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (40% EtOAc in hexanes, Rf = 0.25 in 30%
EtOAc/hexanes) to yield the product, 4. Yield 54 mg, 0.25 mmol, 96%. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.33-7.29 (m, 3H), 5.77 (br s,
1H), 4.46 (d, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H), 2.12-1.95 (m, 2H), 1.90-1.74 (m, 2H), 1.06
(s, 2H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.2, 138.2, 128.9, 128.0, 127.8,
43.9, 30.8, 30.1, 25.6, 20.1; IR (film) 3290, 3055, 2925, 2855, 1756,
1645, 1548, 1454, 1236, 1030, 745, 698 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
